es","\u002Fen\u002Freleases","en\u002F5.releases",[273],{"title":274,"icon":12,"path":275,"stem":276,"children":277,"page":12},"Versions","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions",[278,282,286],{"title":279,"path":280,"stem":281},"v3.2.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-2-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F1.v3-2-0",{"title":283,"path":284,"stem":285},"v3.1.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-1-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F2.v3-1-0",{"title":287,"path":288,"stem":289},"v3.0.0","\u002Fen\u002Freleases\u002Fversions\u002Fv3-0-0","en\u002F5.releases\u002F1.versions\u002F3.v3-0-0",{"id":291,"title":117,"body":292,"description":1236,"extension":1237,"links":1238,"meta":1243,"navigation":1244,"path":118,"seo":1245,"stem":119,"__hash__":1246},"docs_en\u002Fen\u002F3.components\u002F2.text\u002F2.input-number.md",{"type":293,"value":294,"toc":1211},"minimark",[295,303,308,313,336,340,391,395,429,432,568,593,615,619,631,634,653,657,673,676,679,686,689,693,700,703,707,710,726,729,733,740,743,747,767,770,774,787,790,794,801,804,808,812,837,840,916,921,925,962,966,1003,1135,1179,1204,1208],[296,297,298,302],"p",{},[299,300,301],"code",{},"v-model: number | null",".",[304,305,307],"h2",{"id":306},"usage","Usage",[309,310,312],"h3",{"id":311},"decimal-places-and-thousands-separators","Decimal places and thousands separators",[296,314,315,318,319,322,323,326,327,318,330,332,333,335],{},[299,316,317],{},"decimal"," defaults to ",[299,320,321],{},"false",", allowing only integers; a positive integer sets the number of decimal places, and ",[299,324,325],{},"true"," allows any number. ",[299,328,329],{},"thousand-separator",[299,331,325],{},", showing thousands separators on blur; pass ",[299,334,321],{}," for numbers such as years or codes that should not have them.",[337,338],"component-example",{"name":339},"input-number-decimal",[341,342,343,358,371],"ul",{},[344,345,346,347,350,351,354,355,357],"li",{},"While typing, the sign, decimal point and trailing zeros are kept; incomplete input (such as just ",[299,348,349],{},"-",") binds ",[299,352,353],{},"null",". On blur, the value is rounded and padded according to ",[299,356,317],{},", and thousands separators are shown.",[344,359,360,361,363,364,366,367,370],{},"Non-numeric characters and decimals beyond the set places cannot be typed, and pasted text is reverted too. When ",[299,362,317],{}," is ",[299,365,321],{}," or ",[299,368,369],{},"0",", the decimal point cannot be typed.",[344,372,373,374,363,377,380,381,363,383,366,385,387,388,390],{},"On focus, the text switches to the editable form without separators. ",[299,375,376],{},"inputmode",[299,378,379],{},"numeric"," when ",[299,382,317],{},[299,384,321],{},[299,386,369],{},", and ",[299,389,317],{}," otherwise, so phones show the matching number keyboard.",[309,392,394],{"id":393},"step-buttons","Step buttons",[296,396,397,400,401,404,405,408,409,412,413,416,417,420,421,424,425,428],{},[299,398,399],{},"buttons"," shows increment and decrement buttons (off by default), ",[299,402,403],{},"step"," is the amount per step (",[299,406,407],{},"1"," by default), and ",[299,410,411],{},"min",", ",[299,414,415],{},"max"," limit stepping with the buttons and keys. ",[299,418,419],{},"orientation"," sets the button layout: ",[299,422,423],{},"horizontal"," (default) puts decrement on the left and increment on the right and centers the number; ",[299,426,427],{},"vertical"," stacks both on the right and keeps the number right-aligned.",[337,430],{"name":431},"input-number-step",[341,433,434,457,463,480,496,539,551,558],{},[344,435,436,440,441,443,444,412,446,412,448,450,451,453,454,456],{},[437,438,439],"strong",{},"Keyboard",": with ",[299,442,399],{},", or when any of ",[299,445,403],{},[299,447,411],{},[299,449,415],{}," is passed, ArrowUp \u002F ArrowDown steps once in the focused input, PageUp \u002F PageDown steps 10 times, and Home \u002F End jump to ",[299,452,411],{}," \u002F ",[299,455,415],{}," (when set). Without these settings the arrow keys behave as in a normal text input. The buttons are not in the Tab order and are labelled \"Increment\" and \"Decrement\" (following the locale).",[344,458,459,462],{},[437,460,461],{},"Press and hold",": holding a button for more than 0.4 seconds keeps stepping until a limit is reached or the button is released. Pressing a button does not move focus away from the input.",[344,464,465,468,469,471,472,474,475,477,478,302],{},[437,466,467],{},"Empty value",": when the value is ",[299,470,353],{},", both increment and decrement start at ",[299,473,411],{},", or at ",[299,476,369],{}," without ",[299,479,411],{},[344,481,482,485,486,489,490,493,494,302],{},[437,483,484],{},"No floating-point errors",": steps are computed in decimal, so repeatedly adding ",[299,487,488],{},"0.25"," never gives ",[299,491,492],{},"0.7500000001","; the result is rounded to the places allowed by ",[299,495,317],{},[344,497,498,505,506,508,509,511,512,514,515,517,518,520,521,523,524,526,527,529,530,532,533,535,536,538],{},[437,499,500,502,503],{},[299,501,403],{}," and ",[299,504,317],{},": when ",[299,507,403],{}," has more decimal places than ",[299,510,317],{}," allows (for example ",[299,513,488],{}," with ",[299,516,317],{}," set to ",[299,519,321],{},"), the step is rounded to what ",[299,522,317],{}," allows (at least one smallest unit, ",[299,525,407],{}," for ",[299,528,321],{},") with a console warning. A ",[299,531,403],{}," that is not a number above 0, or a ",[299,534,411],{}," greater than ",[299,537,415],{},", is also ignored with a warning.",[344,540,541,544,545,547,548,550],{},[437,542,543],{},"Limits",": the increment button is disabled when the value is at or above ",[299,546,415],{},", and the decrement button at or below ",[299,549,411],{},". Both are disabled while disabled, loading, in a skeleton or in a disabled form.",[344,552,553,554,557],{},"Each step triggers the ",[299,555,556],{},"UFormField"," input and change validation, just like typing.",[344,559,560,502,562,564,565,302],{},[299,561,399],{},[299,563,419],{}," can have site-wide defaults, for example to show the buttons across the project: ",[299,566,567],{},"shuoUi.components.inputNumber.buttons: true",[569,570,571,502,573,575,576,579,580,502,583,586,587,592],"warning",{},[299,572,411],{},[299,574,415],{}," only limit the buttons and keys. ",[437,577,578],{},"A typed value outside the range is not corrected","; the bound value stays as typed, and stepping from it moves back into the range. Keep validating the range in the schema with ",[299,581,582],{},"v.minValue",[299,584,585],{},"v.maxValue","; see ",[588,589,591],"a",{"href":590},"#with-form-validation","With form validation"," below.",[296,594,595,596,453,599,602,603,606,607,610,611,614],{},"In horizontal layout the decrement button takes the place of the left ",[299,597,598],{},"icon",[299,600,601],{},"leadingIcon"," (the ",[299,604,605],{},"#leading"," slot still follows the button); use ",[299,608,609],{},"orientation=\"vertical\""," when you need a left icon. The increment button sits to the right of the unit, the ",[299,612,613],{},"#trailing"," slot and the loading icon, and the padding on both sides follows their actual width, so the number and unit are never pushed out.",[309,616,618],{"id":617},"unit","Unit",[296,620,621,622,363,624,626,627,630],{},"When ",[299,623,617],{},[299,625,325],{},", \"NTD\" is shown (\"元\" in Traditional Chinese, switching with the locale). The text can be changed in ",[588,628,47],{"href":629},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fmessages#overridable-items","; passing a string shows that text. Units vary in length, so the right padding follows the unit's actual width and the number never overlaps the unit.",[337,632],{"name":633},"input-number-unit",[296,635,636,502,638,640,641,645,646,648,649,453,651,302],{},[299,637,617],{},[299,639,329],{}," can also have site-wide defaults; see ",[588,642,644],{"href":643},"\u002Fgetting-started\u002Ftheme\u002Fcomponent-defaults#configurable-props","Configurable props",". The site-wide ",[299,647,617],{}," only accepts ",[299,650,325],{},[299,652,321],{},[309,654,656],{"id":655},"variants","Variants",[296,658,659,660,412,663,502,666,669,670,302],{},"Uses the ",[299,661,662],{},"variant",[299,664,665],{},"color",[299,667,668],{},"highlight"," of ",[299,671,672],{},"UInput",[337,674],{"name":675},"input-number-variant",[309,677,678],{"id":598},"Icon",[296,680,659,681,669,683,685],{},[299,682,598],{},[299,684,672],{},", shown on the left alongside the unit.",[337,687],{"name":688},"input-number-icon",[309,690,692],{"id":691},"size-and-states","Size and states",[296,694,695,696,699],{},"While loading, the spinner sits to the right of the unit and the number and unit move left to make room. See ",[588,697,102],{"href":698},"\u002Fcomponents\u002Foverview\u002Fcommon"," for the behavior shared by all states.",[337,701],{"name":702},"input-number-states",[304,704,706],{"id":705},"examples","Examples",[309,708,591],{"id":709},"with-form-validation",[296,711,712,713,716,717,502,719,721,722,725],{},"Use ",[299,714,715],{},"requiredNumber"," for required fields and add ranges with ",[299,718,582],{},[299,720,585],{},"; use ",[299,723,724],{},"optionalNonNegativeNumber"," for optional non-negative numbers. What gets validated and submitted is a number, without separators.",[337,727],{"name":728},"input-number-validation",[309,730,732],{"id":731},"step-buttons-with-validation","Step buttons with validation",[296,734,735,502,737,739],{},[299,736,411],{},[299,738,415],{}," do not replace validation: the buttons in this example only stop at 0, and the schema checks the upper limit; stepping above 40 shows the error right away.",[337,741],{"name":742},"input-number-step-validation",[309,744,746],{"id":745},"centered-numbers","Centered numbers",[296,748,749,752,753,756,757,760,761,763,764,766],{},[299,750,751],{},"ui.base",